From: zhanghaotian <zhanghaotian@uniontech.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 15:33:00 +0800
Subject: feat: Reduce pixel clock for specific displays to fix black
 screen

Certain display mode combinations cause a black screen because the pixel
clock is not accepted by the hardware.  Apply a small clock reduction at
modeset time only for the targeted displays, identified by their EDID
vendor and product id, so other monitors are unaffected.

The quirk table is built-in and can be disabled via xorg.conf Option
"ClockReduction" (default on).
---
 src/amdgpu_drv.h      |   5 ++
 src/amdgpu_kms.c      |   5 ++
 src/drmmode_display.c | 112 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 122 insertions(+)

